# C Code Review (API & Implementation)

Use this checklist when **reviewing** or **finishing** C headers and sources. Layout and general logging rules are defined in `esp-adf-internal/.cursor/rules/c-coding-style.mdc`; this file adds **review-specific** gates.

---

## Error codes and file layout

- [ ] **Error return definitions** for the module (macros, enums, or dedicated error space) live in a **dedicated header** (or clearly separated dedicated file), not mixed into unrelated headers.
- [ ] **Header** structure follows `c-coding-style.mdc` → *Header Files* (section order, guards, includes, `extern "C"`, typedefs, public API).
- [ ] **Source** structure follows `c-coding-style.mdc` → *Source Files* (includes, locals, statistics, forwards, implementations).

---

## Return type contract

- [ ] **Return type is `esp_err_t`** for status-only results. **Do not** use the return value to pass output data; use `out` parameters, structs, or separate accessors.
- [ ] Header Doxygen lists **every** return code the implementation can return for that function — **complete and accurate** (no missing codes, no obsolete codes).

---

## Doxygen `@return` alignment

- [ ] After `@return`, each line uses: ` *       - <CODE>  <description>`.
- [ ] **Align descriptions** to one column: take the **longest** return token in that block, then add **two spaces**; all description text starts at that column.
- [ ] The **success** line description starts with an **uppercase** letter (e.g. `On success`).
- [ ] **Error** lines describe the condition (e.g. `If svc is NULL`), aligned to the same column as other descriptions.

Example (longest token `ESP_ERR_INVALID_ARG` sets the description column):

```c
 * @return
 *       - ESP_OK                     On success
 *       - ESP_ERR_INVALID_ARG        If svc is NULL
 *       - ESP_ERR_NO_MEM             If allocation fails
```

---

## Includes

- [ ] **Include only what is used** in each `.h` and `.c`. Remove unused `#include` lines.
- [ ] Keep **include order** consistent with `c-coding-style.mdc` (stdlib → FreeRTOS → ESP-IDF → project).

---

## No function comments in source (`.c`)

- [ ] **Do not** add any description, summary, or explanation for a function in `.c` files — no prose above the function, no `@brief`, no block-comment header stating what the function does. All contract documentation belongs in the corresponding `.h` declaration.
- [ ] **Do not** add Doxygen, block comments, or `//` banners **above function definitions** in `.c` files (public or `static`). Document the contract in the **header** for public APIs; keep implementations readable without per-function commentary.
- [ ] **Do not** use comments **inside function bodies** to restate what the code does line-by-line. Exception: brief notes **required** by `c-coding-style.mdc` (e.g. `/* helper already logged */`) or unavoidable non-obvious invariants — keep those minimal and in English.

---

## Error-path logging (public API)

- [ ] For each **user-facing** function, **each** error return path has **exactly one** `ESP_LOGE` or `ESP_LOGW` immediately reflecting that failure (not zero logs; avoid duplicate logs on the same path).
- [ ] Message content should **map cleanly** to the returned `esp_err_t` so logs and return codes match during triage.
- [ ] Respect exceptions documented in `c-coding-style.mdc` (e.g. callee already logged — short comment; avoid noisy logs on documented hot paths).

---

## Quick cross-checks

- [ ] No silent `return` on error without a log (unless explicitly exempted per style guide).
- [ ] Public symbols and Doxygen in `.h` stay in sync with `.c` behaviour.
